export const GATES_README: string = "# Gates\n\nEvery claim Cast Forecast makes goes through a written gate first. Each gate states its pass rule before the data exists, and the result is kept whichever way it lands.\n\n| Gate | Question | Rule written before data | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Gate 1 | Does a film model measured over black and white backgrounds predict on-skin whitening better than the label's zinc percentage? (PLOS ONE 2025 raw data, 13 volunteers, held out by person and by formulation) | Header of [analysis/gate1/heldout_test.py](../../analysis/gate1/heldout_test.py). The rule text was in the header before the first run on 2026-10-27; the script itself was committed to this repository after the run. | FAIL: film model 4.79 L* mean error vs label model 1.61. Exploratory only: on the one differently formulated product, a one-parameter film model missed by 0.69 L* vs the label's 2.35. [gate1-results.md](gate1-results.md) |\n| K2 | Is YouCam's skin tone analysis a usable measurement of the colour in a photo? | Module docstring of `castforecast/k2_tone.py`, committed at [043293a](https://github.com/StephenSook/cast-forecast/blob/043293acc84c72420c922877d3c38fa1c5d844a5/castforecast/k2_tone.py) before the run, with two pre-data amendments at 53e3882 | FAIL 2 of 3: identical result on a fresh upload (pass), but it moved only 0.15x as much as the measured cheek when the photo was made 10 percent brighter, and it sits 15.1 dE00 from the measured cheek. Reading, not pre-registered: it reports a lighting-normalized tone. [k2-results.md](k2-results.md) |\n| K1 | Can YouCam Makeup VTO render a sunscreen-like film, with coverage as the dose? | Module docstring of `castforecast/k1_render.py` at [14a283a](https://github.com/StephenSook/cast-forecast/blob/14a283afc908c8506320b40983c477731bba4aac/castforecast/k1_render.py), with pre-data amendments in the code at [808cdea](https://github.com/StephenSook/cast-forecast/commit/808cdea3d48cffd58a8925682b59419172296a85) | FAIL on 4 of 5: L* reversals at coverage 60 in 3 of 6 series, max dL* 12.7 < 15, inverse dE00 2.03 > 2.0, texture 0.556 < 0.80; R^2 0.954 passed. Post hoc reading (not pre-registered): colorIntensity, not coverage, acted as the dose. [k1-results.md](k1-results.md) |\n| K1b | Same question with colorIntensity as the dose and coverage as texture | [k1b-preregistration.md](k1b-preregistration.md), committed and pushed before any K1b render | PASS 5 of 5. [k1b-results.md](k1b-results.md) |\n\nPublished result files are sanitized by `scripts/publish_results.py` (no file or task ids, URLs, local paths or original photo sizes), and `tests/test_published_results.py` checks every JSON here for those patterns.\n\nSources: Maldonado Lopez et al., PLOS ONE 2025, doi 10.1371/journal.pone.0319891; raw data Mendeley Data jfpzx7hcz2 v2.\n";
